Hello.

1. IDE HDD
- Compaq uses Segate or Fujissu or Maxtor hdd by OEM. Therefore you can buy 
IDE hdd from segate. The difference between Compaq HDD pard and third party 
hdd is only 'Compaq' logo. After you install any IDE hdd, you can set the 
performance by 'hdparm' command.

2. Network Device
- If you want to install gigabit ethernet device in Linux for Alpha, I 
suggest you buy the one use DP chipset. Asante (http://www.asante.com) 
Giganix 1000TPC is suitable for performance and price. You can do it with 
2.4.18 kernel by compiling dp module in kernel source. Asante's 65120-2G 
and 12G gigabit network switch is suitable for your configuration.

