Maybe the redhat install goes into vesa or vga mode which isn't supported
by your graphic card.
Which do you use?
You can boot into interactive mode by typing this at SRM:

>>> boot dva0 -fl i

next you should load the kernel manually when aboot prompts and specify
vga mode normal

aboot> b /vmlinuz vga=normal

or boot /path/to/vmlinuz-whaterver... my memory could be faulty... hope it
works! :) BTW: why not debian? Redhat Linux AXP is dead and resurrected
