Excuse me for this new message!

This is the last.

I have finally got the solution thanks to Michal Jaegermann. The problem was
that I had dd'ed the floppy images into an existing FAT file system which is
prone to error as it creates a new file system on top of the old with the
same space as the floppy and where any wrong bit may cause the problem, though
it does not affect to the files which are going to be used.

So, the solution, just in case it can be useful to another guy, consists in:

1) Recreating a FAT16 file system in the whole /dev/sda1 partition with the
mkdosfs tool. Of course, everything inside it is deleted during the proccess.

2) Copy the files that one is going to use (ldmilo.exe and milo to me) from
the working floppy into the newly created partition. It can be made as much
as by mount'ing and cp'ing as by mcopy'ing without mounting.
