Hi,
Is your RH 7.1 kernel a 2.4.x? I suppose it is, because that would explain
why Milo won't load it. It's because machines like the XL-300 (I have one
myself, running RH7.1; it CAN be done!) need to have
LEGACY_START_ADDRESS=YES (or something similar; anyone correct me!) included
in the kernel. This can only be done by compiling your own kernel from
source (e.g. 2.4.9-31 works for me).
I suggest you upgrade to RH 7.0 (with kernel 2.2.19) and from there start
compiling your own 2.4.x kernel. If that works, upgrade to 7.1.

Guus

