I ran into this same error when doing a RH7.2 install to an
Intel machine.  You can get this message when the installation
is incomplete, as in one or more bad RPM file.  Before RH7.3,
install failures don't seem to get reported in the graphics
install mode.  (Now you get a pop up that hangs you out to
dry, but you can verify the CDs before installation).

I copied iso images on a Windows machine with some write 
errors to a 4 MByte block used as buffer space.  (Really 
makes you want a machine with at least parity).  I installed
the rpms manually and tripped accross errors.

The moral is, your XFree86 may not be completely installed.


